## Why This Is Asked

Tests for optimistic UI and offline resilience are common in messaging apps. This question probes ability to design deterministic E2E tests that cover front-end and back-end coordination, error paths, and data isolation.

## Key Concepts

- Optimistic UI updates
- Network fault simulation and retry handling
- Test data isolation and deterministic seeding
- Front-end/back-end state reconciliation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright test snippet (simplified)
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('delete with optimistic update and Undo', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('https://chat.app');
  await page.fill('#newMessage', 'hello world');
  await page.click('#send');
  const msg = page.locator('.message').last();
  await expect(msg).toHaveText('hello world');

  await msg.click('.delete');
  await expect(page.locator('.toast-undo')).toBeVisible();
  await expect(page.locator('.message')).not.toContainText('hello world');

  await page.click('.toast-undo');
  await expect(page.locator('.message')).toContainText('hello world');
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this to handle multiple concurrent deletions in a single channel?
- How would you verify backend state during intermittent connectivity without flaky tests?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests for feature flags coupled with onboarding flows ensure correct gating, deterministic environments, and resilience to network issues. It checks seeding, isolation, and cleanup in addition to UI correctness.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags and API-driven toggles
- Test data seeding and environment isolation
- End-to-end UI assertions for multi-step flows
- Network fault simulation and idempotent retries
- Cleanup and restoration of test state

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright example sketch
const { test, expect } = require('@playwright/test');

test('new-onboarding flow gated by feature flag', async ({ request, page }) => {
  // enable flag for test user
  await request.post('/api/flags', { data: { userId: 'test-user', flag: 'new-onboarding', value: true } });
  // seed data and start session
  await request.post('/api/tests/seed', { data: { userId: 'test-user', env: 'e2e' } });
  await page.goto('/onboarding');
  // verify four steps render
  for (let i = 1; i <= 4; i++) {
    await expect(page.locator(`#step-${i}`)).toBeVisible();
    await page.click(`#step-${i}-next`);
  }
  // final dashboard
  await expect(page).toHaveURL('/dashboard');
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you run this test across multiple browsers concurrently?
- How would you rollback the flag if tests fail in CI?

